 "flags": [
  "Crosswalk is labelled NIST but was contributed by Microsoft; NIST hosts it with a no-endorsement disclaimer. Based on ISO/IEC FDIS 42001, not the published 2023 text.",
  "Crosswalk cites Annex B guidance numbers (B.x.y) not Annex A control numbers; iso_annex_a_equiv is a derived renumbering.",
  "MAP 1.4 prints 'B.2.2 Customers': B.2.2 is AI policy elsewhere in the same document and Customers is B.10.4. Kept as printed (B.2.2); likely a source error.",
  "MAP 1.5 prints '6.1.1 Objective'; the clause title is 6.1.1 General. Number kept.",
  "Crosswalk prints '5.2 AI Policy' (capital P) and 'Monitoring, measurement, analysis, and evaluation' (serial comma); minor typographic differences from clause titles.",
  "Crosswalk extraction was done via a summarizing fetch tool; GOVERN, MAP 1.4, 1.5, 4.1 re-fetched verbatim and matched. Other rows single-pass; spot-check against the PDF before publishing.",
  "A.5.4: 'individuals or groups of individuals' (mindsetcyber, deepinspect; toolkit has abbreviated 'individuals or groups') vs crosswalk FDIS text 'individuals and groups of individuals'. Used 'or'.",
  "A.10.2: 'Allocating responsibilities' (crosswalk, deepinspect, ISMS.online page title) vs 'Allocation of responsibilities' (mindsetcyber, iso42001toolkit). Used 'Allocating'.",
  "A.8 group title: 'Information for interested parties of AI systems' (mindsetcyber, deepinspect) vs 'Information for interested parties' (iso42001toolkit). Used the longer form.",
  "A.6.2.8: iso42001toolkit abbreviates to 'AI system event logs'; others and crosswalk give 'AI system recording of event logs'.",
  "Minor singular/plural and organisation/organization variants across sources (A.6.1.2, A.7.2, A.9.3 'AI system' vs 'AI systems'; A.2.3, A.3). Used the form matching the crosswalk and deepinspect; ISO publishes in -ization spelling.",
  "iso.org OBP preview and ISMS.online pages render via JavaScript and could not be read; the ISO text itself was not checked.",
  "Clause subclauses 7.5.1, 7.5.2, 9.2.1, 9.3.1-9.3.3 confirmed in cyberzoni plus crosswalk (9.x) only; 7.5.1/7.5.2 single-source (follow the ISO Harmonized Structure)."
